WEBVTT

00:00:59.688 --> 00:01:01.901
and this is how the nuclear reactor today works.

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:03.310
It works pretty good.

00:01:03.310 --> 00:01:05.464
And then there's fusion.

00:01:05.464 --> 00:01:07.870
Now, I like fusion. Fusion's much better.

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:09.564
So you take two small nuclei,

00:01:09.564 --> 00:01:12.070
you put it together, and you make helium,

00:01:12.070 --> 00:01:13.428
and that's very nice.

00:01:13.428 --> 00:01:14.974
It makes lots of energy.

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:17.574
This is nature's way of producing energy.

00:01:17.574 --> 00:01:19.982
The sun and all the stars in the universe

00:01:19.982 --> 00:01:22.227
run on fusion.

00:01:22.227 --> 00:01:24.123
Now, a fusion plant

00:01:24.123 --> 00:01:26.438
would actually be quite cost-effective

00:01:26.438 --> 00:01:28.428
and it also would be quite safe.

00:01:28.428 --> 00:01:32.861
It only produces short term radioactive waste,